  "evidence": "A: NHS capacity boosts (2m extra operations, 40,000 weekly appointments), 8,500 more mental‑health staff, a National Care Service, Warm Homes Plan and tougher water‑company enforcement; strict fiscal rules and no rises to Income Tax/NI/VAT; reduce net migration and tie shortage visas to domestic training; clean power by 2030 without measures like airport moratoria. B: Free personal care and a Carer’s Minimum Wage uplift; abolish the two‑child limit, benefit cap and sanctions, expand free school meals; right to a GP in 7 days; liberalise immigration/asylum (scrap Illegal Migration Act, right to work after 3 months); strong environmental purity measures (Clean Air Act, sewage tax, double nature by 2050, ban short flights <2.5h, moratorium on net airport expansion); new/higher taxes (buyback levy, bank tax reversal, CGT reform).",
